  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "{Straw weaving} ( (草编) ) is an {antique} method of {manufacturing} daily {items} or {artworks} .It was listed as a {national intangible} cultural {heritage} in 2008, for it demonstrates the essence of tradition and the {labor} of skilled workers.The earliest straw-weaving {products} were discovered at Hemudu Site, a Neolithic cultural site {located} in {eastern} China's Zhejiang {Province} .Some of these products are now displayed in {museums} .One can imagine an old {fisherman} sitting under a woven ( (编织的) ) {hat} , crafting straw into complex patterns.",
      "cn": "草编 是一种 制作 日常 用品 或 艺术品 的 古老 工艺。2008年，草编被列为 国家级非物质 文化 遗产 ，因为它展现了传统的精髓和能工巧匠的 劳作 。最早的草编 制品 出土于河姆渡 遗址 ，该遗址 位于 中国 东部的 浙江 省 ，是一处新石器时代的文化遗址。其中一些（草编）制品如今陈列在 博物馆 。人们可以想象，一位老 渔夫 戴着一顶草编 帽子 （即斗笠），正将草编织成复杂的图案。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "One such intangible cultural {inheritor} , Wu Cui, can turn the straw left over from harvested {wheat} into {eye-catching} artworks, such as baskets, hats, and {toys} for children.Wu explains the process of straw weaving: selection of materials is the first step of a {complicated} and {time-consuming} process that can take weeks, or even months, to complete.You need to sketch ( (画素描) ) the piece on paper, soak ( (浸泡) ) the straw and dry it under the {sunny} skies before beginning to weave.Next comes weaving, shaping and preserving of the work.Some artisans would integrate other {fibers} like {cotton} , {wool} , or {gold threads} to add texture ( (质地) ) and color to their works.",
      "cn": "吴翠就是这一非物质文化遗产的 继承人 ，她可以把收割 小麦 剩下的秸秆变成 引人注目的 艺术品，比如篮子、帽子和儿童 玩具 。吴翠解释了草编的过程：草编的过程 复杂 而 耗时 ，可能需要数周甚至数月才能完成，在此过程中，材料的选择是第一步。在开始编织之前，你需要在纸上勾勒出草编的样式，将麦秆浸泡好，然后在 阳光充足的 日子晾干。接下来是作品的编织、塑形和保存。一些工匠会添加 棉 、 羊毛 或 金线 等其他 纤维 ，为他们的作品增添质感和色彩。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "There are only about 100 individuals involved in the work across the country.Cultural organizations are providing {awards} to people willing to learn and continue the practice.“The world has changed, and {craftsmen} need to {transcend practicality} and {pursue} the {beauty} and {artistry} of straw culture to help the {craft} survive and {thrive} ,”Wu says.When asked about her plans in the future, Wu says she will {systematically} study the local traditional culture and create products to express artistic {fantasy} .",
      "cn": "全国只有大约100人从事草编工作。文化机构正在为愿意学习和继续从事这项工作的人提供 奖励 。吴翠说：“世界已经发生了变化， 工匠 们需要 超越实用性 的藩篱， 追求 草编文化的 美感 和 艺术性 ，以帮助这项 工艺 生存和 蓬勃发展 。”当被问及未来的计划时，吴翠表示自己将 系统地 学习当地的传统文化，创造出能表达艺术 幻想 的制品。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
